bal/import/math.*; ternary `n = tile_size if ... else ...` is supported (identical to proven sigmoid template); `asc2.range(..., unroll_factor=2)` only (valid under both contract statements) ✓. No asc-v1 red flags ✓.\n\n**Anti-cheat** — all numerical work (cast, scale, shift, factor-mul, exp, store-cast) inside the kernel ✓; torch only for `empty_like`, `is_contiguous`, `contiguous`, `numel` ✓; `math.log` is host-side scalar attr reduction (allowed; \"NO math.*\" applies inside jit only) ✓; fresh contiguous output, no views, no data_ptr caching ✓.\n\n**UB budget (253952 B)** — Exp chain = 5 f32 intermediates + f16 load + f16 store, structurally identical to the proven sigmoid chain (5 f32). Sigmoid measured 155648 B @2048 and 311296 B @4096 (exactly 2×, linear). Linear interp → ~233K @3072 < 253952 (~20K headroom); sigmoid's measured overhead factor 1.584× applies by structural equivalence. Tile DMA 32-B alignment: 3072×4(f32)=12288, 3072×2(f16/bf16)=6144, both ÷32 ✓. Label: `suspected` (compile gate not runnable in this no-pyasc env) but well-justified; documented fallback 3072→1536→1024 on overflow, never drops cases.\n\nNo fixes required — the candidate is statically correct. Running the only permitted check:","time":{"start":1788347807492,"end":1788347821744}}}
